x86_64-linux  every special member here is defined inside the class, so clang emits one comdat copy as C2/D2 and no C1 or D1 at all where cxx1 emits both of Itanium's forms - see docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol". Nothing here is about moves: the extra names are S's constructor and destructor forms, not the move constructor's spelling, and arm64-darwin agrees with clang on all 8 names while x86_64-windows agrees on all of its own
